1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,660
We owe a lot to cities.
我们在很多方面受惠于城市。

2
00:00:03,660 --> 00:00:12,200
These densely populated hubs of transit, industry and commerce brought together great swathes of the population.
这些人口稠密的交通、工业和商业枢纽，汇聚了大量人口。

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:28,970
More than just living together for safety, cities allowed people to cooperate more easily and, as a result, develop more complex societies, science, and culture – things we continue to benefit from today.
城市的意义不止于让人们为了安全聚居，更让人们得以更便捷地协作，进而发展出更复杂的社会、科学和文化——我们今天仍从中受益。

4
00:00:28,970 --> 00:00:36,860
In 2016 the UN revealed that over 50% of the world's population live in urban settlements.
2016年，联合国公布的数据显示，全球超过50%的人口居住在城镇区域。

5
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:41,090
Of these cities, 31 are classified as megacities.
在这些城市中，有31座被归类为特大城市。

6
00:00:41,090 --> 00:00:46,010
A megacity is one where its inhabitants number more than 10 million.
特大城市指的是人口超过1000万的城市。

7
00:00:46,010 --> 00:00:50,820
And globally this trend is expected to increase.
而且从全球范围来看，这一趋势预计还会持续加剧。

8
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:53,870
London is no exception.
伦敦也不例外。

9
00:00:53,870 --> 00:01:07,750
Unsurprisingly, as England's capital city, London has a population of over 10 million – up by 1.1 million since 2008, according to one BBC article.
英国广播公司的一篇报道称，作为英格兰的首都，伦敦人口已超过1000万，自2008年以来增长了110万，这一结果并不出人意料。

10
00:01:07,750 --> 00:01:15,470
This is a result of a higher birth rate than mortality rate, and an increase in international immigration.
人口增长得益于出生率高于死亡率，以及国际移民数量的增加。

11
00:01:15,470 --> 00:01:25,610
However, despite these rises, half a million more people have migrated away from this metropolis than have flocked to it.
然而，尽管人口出现增长，从这座大都市迁出的人口还是比涌入的人口多出了50万。

12
00:01:25,610 --> 00:01:28,220
Why might this be?
这背后的原因是什么呢？

13
00:01:28,220 --> 00:01:31,340
It's the result of age.
这是由年龄因素造成的。

14
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:47,720
Where members of all other age groups tend to depart more than they arrive, young people between the ages of 20 and 30 are drawn to the range and number of jobs that the city offers and the education opportunities that can be found there.
其他所有年龄段的人口迁出数量往往多于迁入数量，而20至30岁的年轻人则被这座城市丰富多样的就业岗位和教育机会所吸引。

15
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:56,890
This explains why London has one of the youngest average populations in the UK, just 37, according to the BBC.
英国广播公司称，这也解释了为什么伦敦是英国平均年龄最低的地区之一，仅为37岁。

16
00:01:56,890 --> 00:01:59,860
And the rest of the country?
那么英国其他地区的情况如何呢？

17
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:19,580
From 2002 to 2015 municipalities such as Liverpool, Birmingham and Manchester saw a population growth of 181%, 163% and 149% respectively, according to figures from the Office for National Statistics.
英国国家统计局的数据显示，2002年至2015年间，利物浦、伯明翰和曼彻斯特等城市的人口增长率分别达到了181%、163%和149%。

18
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:29,380
Young professionals looking for high-paying jobs are attracted to the opportunities provided by growth in sectors such as finance and law.
寻求高薪工作的年轻职场人士，被金融和法律等行业发展所带来的机会吸引而来。

19
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:39,630
This in turn causes the development of city amenities such as gyms, restaurants and bars, making it an even more attractive place to live.
这反过来又推动了健身房、餐厅和酒吧等城市配套设施的建设，让这些地方变得更宜居。

20
00:02:39,630 --> 00:02:43,690
So are people in the UK leaving cities?
那么英国人是否在离开城市呢？

21
00:02:43,690 --> 00:02:46,080
It depends on where you look.
答案取决于具体地区。

22
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:53,670
What does seem clear is that people's views on the advantages of urban living may change as they get older.
但有一点似乎很明确：人们对城市生活优势的看法会随着年龄的增长而改变。

23
00:02:53,670 --> 00:02:58,845
Where once was opportunity, now there may be hassle.
曾经充满机遇的地方，如今或许只剩下嘈杂与困扰。

24
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:02,720
Has your relationship with a city changed over time?
你与一座城市的关系是否也会随着时间而改变呢？
